				<div class="et_pb_code_inner"><style is:inline set:html={__c0}></style><div class="azc"><span class="azc-updated">Updated October 2026</span><h2>How Much Does a New HVAC System Cost in Frisco &amp; Little Elm?</h2><div class="azc-answer"><p>A complete HVAC system replacement in Frisco, Little Elm and the greater Dallas–Fort Worth area typically costs <strong>$8,000–$16,000 installed in 2026</strong>. Most homeowners replacing a standard system with existing ductwork should budget around <strong>$9,000–$13,000</strong>, depending on the equipment and installation.</p> </div><h3>2026 HVAC Replacement Costs by System Type</h3><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Estimated installed cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>AC system only</strong><small>Outdoor condenser and indoor evaporator coil</small></td><td class="azc-price">$7,000–$13,500</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Furnace replacement only</strong><small>New furnace with standard installation</small></td><td class="azc-price">$3,500–$7,500</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Complete HVAC system</strong><small>AC, furnace or air handler, and installation</small></td><td class="azc-price">$8,000–$16,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Premium high-efficiency system</strong><small>Variable-speed equipment and advanced comfort features</small></td><td class="azc-price">$13,000–$20,000+</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="azc-note">Estimated installed prices. Actual costs depend on equipment size, brand, labor and existing system conditions.</p> </div></div>
