				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_code et_pb_code_1">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_code_inner"><div class="azc"><h2>AC Replacement Cost by System Size</h2><p>For a standard-efficiency central AC system with existing ductwork, these are approximate 2026 installation prices in the DFW area. Not sure what size your home needs? Our <a href="/air-conditioning-installation/">AC installation team</a> sizes every system before quoting.</p> <table><thead><tr><th>System size</th><th>Typical installed cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>2 ton</strong></td><td class="azc-price">$6,500–$10,500</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2.5 ton</strong></td><td class="azc-price">$7,000–$11,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3 ton</strong></td><td class="azc-price">$7,500–$12,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3.5 ton</strong></td><td class="azc-price">$8,000–$13,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4 ton</strong></td><td class="azc-price">$9,000–$14,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5 ton</strong></td><td class="azc-price">$10,000–$16,000+</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="azc-note">A high-efficiency system can cost several thousand dollars more than a standard model.</p> </div></div>
