				<div class="et_pb_code_inner"><div class="azc"><h2>What Affects Your HVAC Replacement Cost?</h2><div class="azc-grid"><div class="azc-card"><h3>Equipment Size</h3><p>Larger homes need higher-tonnage systems, which cost more to buy and install.</p> </div><div class="azc-card"><h3>Brand &amp; Efficiency</h3><p>Premium, variable-speed and high-efficiency equipment can add several thousand dollars over a standard model.</p> </div><div class="azc-card"><h3>Your Existing System</h3><p>The condition of your ductwork, electrical and current setup, plus labor and permits, all affect the final price.</p> </div></div><h3 style="margin-top:36px">Ways to Lower Your Cost</h3><p>Check our <a href="/coupon-specials/">current specials</a> for offers on new system installations, and see our <a href="/financing/">financing options</a> to spread the cost into manageable payments. Replacing both units at once? Read <a href="/replace-ac-and-furnace-together/">whether to replace your AC and furnace together</a>.</p> </div></div>
