				<div class="et_pb_code_inner"><div class="azc azc-faq"><h2 class="azc-center">HVAC Replacement Cost FAQs</h2><details><summary>How much does it cost to replace an HVAC system in Frisco, TX?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>A complete HVAC system replacement in Frisco and the greater DFW area typically costs $8,000–$16,000 installed in 2026. Most homeowners replacing a standard system with existing ductwork should budget around $9,000–$13,000.</p> </div></details><details><summary>How much does a new AC unit cost in Little Elm, TX?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>Replacing an AC system only, meaning the outdoor condenser and indoor evaporator coil, typically costs $7,000–$13,500 installed. A premium high-efficiency system can run $13,000–$20,000 or more.</p> </div></details><details><summary>How much does a 3-ton AC system cost to install?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>A standard-efficiency 3-ton central AC system with existing ductwork typically costs $7,500–$12,000 installed in the DFW area. A 4-ton system runs about $9,000–$14,000, and a 5-ton system about $10,000–$16,000 or more.</p> </div></details><details><summary>How much does furnace replacement cost?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>Replacing a furnace only, with standard installation, typically costs $3,500–$7,500 in North Texas.</p> </div></details><details><summary>Do I need new ductwork when I replace my HVAC system?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>Not always. If your existing ducts are in good shape, they can usually be reused. Duct repairs or modifications typically cost $500–$3,000, and full ductwork replacement typically costs $1,500–$6,000.</p> </div></details><details><summary>Do I need a permit to replace my HVAC system?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>Permits and inspections are a potential added cost, typically $75–$500, depending on the job.</p> </div></details><details><summary>How much more does a high-efficiency HVAC system cost?</summary><div class="azc-a"><p>A high-efficiency system can cost several thousand dollars more than a standard model. Premium high-efficiency systems with variable-speed equipment typically cost $13,000–$20,000 or more installed.</p> </div></details></div><script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={__c1}></script></div>
			</div>
